    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i like the \"compelling preliminary evidence\" angle. but i'm worried some of these investors are going to be real sticklers for the math. if they ask me point-blank if we reached statistical significance, i don't want to sound like i'm dodging the question or being vague. can you help me draft a specific sentence or two for the \"Results\" slide that communicates a successful finding without explicitly lying about the p-value?",
